.\" Man page for wifi-hotspot.  View with:  man ./man/wifi-hotspot.8
.TH WIFI-HOTSPOT 8 "October 2026" "wifi-hotspot 1.1.2" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
wifi-hotspot \- share a Wi-Fi connection as a hotspot while staying connected
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo wifi-hotspot
.RB { start | stop | restart }
.br
.B sudo wifi-hotspot
.RB { ssid
.IR NAME | \c
.B pass
.IR PASSWORD | \c
.B max
.IR N | \c
.B rate
.RI [ MBIT ] | \c
.B security
.IR MODE }
.br
.B sudo wifi-hotspot
.RB { block | unblock | allow | disallow }
.I MAC
.br
.B sudo wifi-hotspot limit
.I MAC DOWN UP
.br
.B wifi-hotspot
.RB { show | clients | blocked }
.br
.B sudo wifi-hotspot secret
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wifi-hotspot
turns a Linux laptop into a Windows-style "Mobile Hotspot".
It creates a virtual access-point interface,
.BR ap0 ,
next to the Wi-Fi interface that is already connected to the internet, and
shares that connection with other devices.
.PP
It uses
.BR hostapd (8)
for the access point,
.BR dnsmasq (8)
for DHCP and DNS,
.BR iptables (8)
for NAT and firewalling, and
.BR tc (8)
for speed limits.
Firewall rules live in their own chains
.RB ( HS_IN ", " HS_FWD ", " HS_NAT ", " HS_ACCT ),
so they are added and removed cleanly without touching other rules.
.PP
The access point always uses the same channel and band as the network the
laptop is connected to, because a single radio can only be on one channel.
If that network changes channel, the hotspot restarts on the new one.
If the Wi-Fi connection is lost for about 24 seconds, the hotspot stops.
.PP
Commands that change settings, start or stop the hotspot, or reveal the
password must be run as root.
.BR show ", " clients " and " blocked
work as a normal user.
Most setting changes are saved right away but take effect only after
.BR restart .
.PP
The graphical front end,
.BR wifi-hotspot-gui (1),
calls this program for every action.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Running the hotspot
.TP
.B start
Create
.BR ap0 ,
start hostapd and dnsmasq, set up the firewall and NAT, and start the
background watcher.
Prints the network name, channel, upstream interface and subnet.
If hostapd fails, the last lines of its log are printed.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the hotspot, remove
.BR ap0 ,
and remove every firewall and traffic-shaping rule it added.
It is safe to run when the hotspot is already stopped.
.TP
.B restart
Run
.B stop
and then
.BR start .
Use it to apply changed settings.
.SS Settings
.TP
.BI ssid " NAME"
Set the network name.
.TP
.BI pass " PASSWORD"
Set the Wi-Fi password: 8 to 63 characters, and it must not contain
.RB \(dq | \(dq.
.TP
.BI max " N"
Set the maximum number of connected devices.
.TP
.BR rate " [\fIMBIT\fR]"
Set a download speed limit in Mbit/s shared by the whole hotspot.
With no value, the limit is removed.
.TP
.BI security " MODE"
Set the security mode:
.B wpa2
(the default, works with every device),
.B wpa2wpa3
(mixed mode), or
.B wpa3
(WPA3 only; older devices cannot connect).
.SS Devices
.I MAC
is a device's hardware address, like
.BR aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff .
Upper or lower case is accepted.
While the hotspot is running, changes take effect immediately.
.TP
.BI block " MAC"
Add the device to the block list and disconnect it if it is connected.
It is also removed from the approved list.
.TP
.BI unblock " MAC"
Remove the device from the block list.
.TP
.BI allow " MAC"
Add the device to the approved list (and remove it from the block list).
The approved list only matters when approved-only mode
.RB ( ALLOWLIST=1 )
is on.
.TP
.BI disallow " MAC"
Remove the device from the approved list.
If approved-only mode is on, the device is disconnected.
.TP
.BI limit " MAC DOWN UP"
Limit one device's download and upload speeds, in Mbit/s (0\(en1000).
.B "limit"
.I MAC
.B "0 0"
removes the limit.
.SS Information
.TP
.B show
Print the current settings as
.IB KEY = VALUE
lines, including the channel, the upstream interface and, while running,
the total data used.
It never prints the password.
.TP
.B clients
Print one line per connected device, with these tab-separated fields:
MAC, IP address, host name, bytes downloaded, bytes uploaded, download
limit and upload limit.
Prints nothing when the hotspot is off.
.TP
.B blocked
Print the block list, one MAC address per line.
.TP
.B secret
Print the Wi-Fi password.
Requires root.
.SS Internal commands
These are used by the GUI and the installer.
You normally don't need them.
.TP
.B apply \fISSID MAX RATE SECURITY ISOLATE ALLOWLIST IDLE_MIN CAP_MB NOTIFY \fR[\fISHOW_PANEL_ICON\fR]
Check and save all settings at once, and restart the hotspot if it is
running.
A new password can be given as the first line of standard input; an
empty line keeps the current one.
.TP
.B init
Create the configuration files if they are missing and generate a random
password.
Existing settings are kept.
.TP
.B watch
The background loop started by
.BR start .
It writes live statistics, enforces the idle timeout and data cap, and
follows changes in the upstream Wi-Fi.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are stored in
.I /etc/hotspot.conf
as
.IB KEY = VALUE
lines.
.TP
.B SSID
Network name (1\(en32 bytes).
The default is
.IB hostname -Hotspot\fR.
.TP
.B MAXCLIENTS
Maximum number of devices (1\(en32, default 8).
.TP
.B RATE
Download limit for the whole hotspot, in Mbit/s; empty means no limit.
.TP
.B SECURITY
.BR wpa2 " (default), " wpa2wpa3 " or " wpa3 .
.TP
.B ISOLATE
If 1, connected devices cannot reach each other.
.TP
.B ALLOWLIST
If 1, only devices on the approved list can connect (approved-only mode).
.TP
.B IDLE_MIN
Turn off the hotspot after this many minutes with no devices connected (0 = never).
.TP
.B CAP_MB
Turn off the hotspot after this many megabytes in total (0 = no limit).
.TP
.B NOTIFY
If 1, show a desktop notification when devices join or leave.
.TP
.B SHOW_PANEL_ICON
If 1, the GNOME Shell extension shows a panel icon.
.PP
These optional keys are detected automatically if not set:
.TP
.B STA
The Wi-Fi interface connected to the internet, for example
.BR wlan0 .
.TP
.B COUNTRY
Two-letter regulatory country code, for example
.BR IN .
.TP
.B SUBNET
The first three parts of the hotspot's IPv4 subnet, for example
.BR 192.168.50 .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hotspot.conf
Settings (readable by everyone; it never contains the password).
.TP
.I /etc/hotspot.secret
The Wi-Fi password (readable by root only).
.TP
.I /etc/hotspot.deny
Blocked MAC addresses, one per line.
.TP
.I /etc/hotspot.allow
Approved MAC addresses, one per line.
.TP
.I /etc/hotspot.limits
Per-device speed limits, one
.RI \(dq "MAC DOWN UP" \(dq
line per device.
.TP
.I /run/hotspot-status
Live statistics written by the watcher, readable by everyone.
.TP
.I /run/hotspot-hostapd.conf\fR, \fI/run/hotspot-hostapd.log
The generated hostapd configuration and its log.
.TP
.I /etc/NetworkManager/conf.d/90-hotspot-ap0.conf
Tells NetworkManager not to manage
.BR ap0 .
.TP
.I /etc/sudoers.d/wifi-hotspot
Lets the installing user run
.BR "wifi-hotspot start" " and " "wifi-hotspot stop"
without a password.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, and non-zero if a value is invalid, the command is not run
as root when it needs to be, or the hotspot fails to start.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the hotspot and show its password:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo wifi-hotspot start
sudo wifi-hotspot secret
.fi
.RE
.PP
Change the name and password, then apply them:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo wifi-hotspot ssid "My Laptop"
sudo wifi-hotspot pass "correct-horse-battery"
sudo wifi-hotspot restart
.fi
.RE
.PP
Limit one device to 5 Mbit/s down and 2 Mbit/s up:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo wifi-hotspot limit aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff 5 2
.fi
.RE
.PP
List connected devices:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wifi-hotspot clients
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
The Wi-Fi card must support being a client and an access point at the same
time.
Check with:
.PP
.RS
.nf
iw list | grep -A8 'valid interface combinations'
.fi
.RE
.PP
The output should show both
.B managed
and
.BR AP .
.PP
The distribution's own
.B hostapd
service is disabled during installation, because
.B wifi-hotspot
runs its own hostapd.
.SH BUGS
Only IPv4 is supported.
An active Wi-Fi connection is required; Ethernet-only internet is not
supported.
Blocking by MAC address can be bypassed by devices that use random MAC
addresses.
.PP
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/SudarsanamR/wifi-hotspot/issues
.UE .
